  "label": "The contemplative man with cigar is mapped as the person who should 'shoot 'em' when hearing 'allahakbar' crap",
  "description": "The visual entity 'contemplative_man_with_cigar' (John Candy) is analogically mapped to the textual role of the person who is instructed to 'shoot 'em' in response to hearing 'allahakbar' crap. This mapping is established by the juxtaposition of the image of a calm, older white man with the violent, hateful text, creating a jarring contrast that implies the man embodies the violent action described. The text does not explicitly say 'you' or 'me', but the visual material is presented as the subject of the instruction, making the man the implicit agent of the violent action described in the text.",
